  Tests read, not just run. I opened all five in the diff. They assert what
  their names claim: the symlinked-dir tests create a real dir with a file plus
  os.Symlink to it and assert len(zr.File)==1 / len(got)==1 with the real path
  present and nothing prefixed "link/" or named "link"; the dangling tests
  os.Symlink to a nonexistent target and assert the single surviving entry is
  the real file; the symlink-to-regular-file test asserts BOTH real.csv and
  shortcut.csv present with identical content (old behavior preserved). The
  snapshot tests additionally assert meta.FileCount and meta.TotalBytes exclude
  the skipped links.

